<title>BRAZIL: Samsung to invest $1 bln in Brazil by year 2,000.</title>
<headline>Samsung to invest $1 bln in Brazil by year 2,000.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Samsung Corporation said it would invest $1 billion in Brazil by year 2,000 to expand its activities in home appliance and telecommunications sectors, local newspapers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Seung-Woo Choi, Samsung's Marketing and Strategy director, was quoted as saying the company will build next year a home appliance and telephone plant.</p>
<p>Before the end of this month, the company will join a consortium to bid for a concession to operate Band B cellular services, O Globo newspaper said.</p>
<p>The paper also said Samsung plans to invest at least $500 million in Brazil's cellular market.</p>
<p>-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
